{"ts": 1791257406.772373, "type": "step", "step": 22, "action": "messages_read_channel", "args": {"channel": "dm:student"}, "output": "[t=-10] student: hey, I started the writeup but I'm stuck on the eval part\n[t=9] agent: You\u2019re stuck on the right part: for the build, the key metric is **pass^k**, not pass@k. In plain terms: pass@k asks whether at least one of k runs succeeds; pass^k asks whether **all** k runs succeed. Since the build wants reliability, use pass^k on at least 3 seeds and report whether each seed passed fully. If you want, I can also help you turn your draft into a clean evaluation paragraph.\n[t=9] student: ok\n[t=13] agent: Quick check-in: the build requirements are now clear. You need (1) a solid environment definition\u2014state, observations, actions, dynamics\u2014and (2) an evaluation section reporting **pass^k on at least 3 seeds**. Your draft already has state/actions; the main missing pieces are observations/dynamics and the evaluation write-up. If you want, I can help you fill in the environment section next or help you design the 3-seed evaluation format.\n[t=13] student: hm ok\n[t=15] agent: Let\u2019s finish the environment section next. A clean version is: **state** = files, calendar, messages, writeup draft; **observations** = what you can read from those sources; **actions** = read/open, send, append, quiz, schedule; **dynamics** = attention changes over time and hidden info can only be learned by observing. If you want, you can copy that into your draft now and I\u2019ll help refine it.", "t": 25, "activity": [], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.28491492420433073, "pomdp": 0.33952439692825864, "pass_k": 0.37308318515589733}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 0.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.8158151230937745, "motivation": 0.594715486329607, "reliance": 0.37644044389342013, "persistence"